# Copy to .env and fill in. scripts/serve.sh and scripts/invite-business.sh load it.
# Signs session tokens and keys secrets at rest. Generate one with:
#   python3 -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"
# Changing it closes every open session.
APOSTROPHE_SECRET_KEY=
# Optional. Defaults to sqlite:///./apostrophe.db
# APOSTROPHE_DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///./apostrophe.db
# Optional. Where users reach the app; invitation links start with it.
# Defaults to http://localhost:8000
# APOSTROPHE_PUBLIC_URL=http://192.168.0.10:8000
# Optional. Defaults to 8000.
# APOSTROPHE_PORT=8000
# Optional. A Turso auth token, passed to the driver as a connect argument, never part
# of APOSTROPHE_DATABASE_URL. Unset on the home network (plain SQLite needs none).
# APOSTROPHE_DATABASE_AUTH_TOKEN=
# Optional, comma-separated CIDRs. The reverse proxy hops whose X-Forwarded-For entry
# the app may trust for the client address (the login brake). Empty on the home
# network, where there is no proxy. Required when APOSTROPHE_PUBLIC_URL is https.
# APOSTROPHE_TRUSTED_PROXIES=10.0.0.0/8
# Optional. Only en-XA is accepted: the test locale, shown everywhere to judge layout.
# Any other value stops startup. Not for production.
# APOSTROPHE_FORCED_LANGUAGE=en-XA
